From: Tobkiri exact-window audit
Base: cua-driver-rs-v0.28.2 (fc188250b4ca8549b8e61f937fdb1fb560770e86)
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] EXPERIMENTAL cua-driver: try a separate AX action timeout

EXPERIMENTAL — do not apply this patch by default. The AX tree walker sets a
two-second timeout on descendants that are then retained in the element cache.
This patch tests the hypothesis that resetting the retained element to a
bounded five-second mutation budget immediately before the single action RPC
avoids an inherited observation timeout.

Five seconds is an unvalidated diagnostic hypothesis, not a proven target
latency. Accept or ship this patch only after signed native acceptance confirms
the intended operation, its timing, and the absence of duplicated effects.

This patch deliberately does not retry: AXUIElementPerformAction runs once and
every non-success result, including kAXErrorCannotComplete and an unknown
completion state, is returned unchanged to the caller.

diff --git a/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-macos/src/ax/bindings.rs b/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-macos/src/ax/bindings.rs
index 02ba09c..1cdfccc 100644
--- a/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-macos/src/ax/bindings.rs
+++ b/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-macos/src/ax/bindings.rs
@@ -573,10 +573,22 @@ pub unsafe fn copy_element_attr(
 
 /// Perform an AX action using a string attribute name.
 ///
+/// The tree walker gives every cached descendant a short two-second messaging
+/// timeout so observation cannot strand a blocking worker. That timeout stays
+/// attached to the retained `AXUIElementRef`. Give the one mutation RPC a
+/// separate bounded budget before dispatch; otherwise a healthy but briefly
+/// busy AppKit target can inherit the observation budget and return
+/// `kAXErrorCannotComplete` before handling `AXPress`.
+///
+/// This does not retry an action. `AXUIElementPerformAction` is invoked exactly
+/// once and its native result is returned unchanged, so a timeout or unknown
+/// completion state is never converted to success or replayed.
 /// # Safety
 ///
 /// `element` must be a valid, live `AXUIElementRef` for the duration of the call.
 pub unsafe fn perform_action(element: AXUIElementRef, action_name: &str) -> AXError {
+    const AX_ACTION_MESSAGING_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: f32 = 5.0;
+    let _ = AXUIElementSetMessagingTimeout(element, AX_ACTION_MESSAGING_TIMEOUT_SECONDS);
     let action = CFStr::new(action_name);
     AXUIElementPerformAction(element, action.as_concrete_TypeRef())
 }
